Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:08:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] feat(skills): append repo_docs files to delivered skill
 instructions

A SKILL.md can declare `repo_docs:` in its frontmatter: one path or a
YAML list (block or inline). When the skill's full instructions reach
the model (read_skill output, instructions inlined in full mode or for
`always` skills) each file is appended after the body as
`--- repo docs: <path> ---` plus its content, or a single
`--- repo docs: <path> (not found) ---` line when unreadable. A leading
`~` expands to the home directory. Files are read at delivery time, so
edits in the repo show up without a reload. Compact summaries and other
frontmatter keys are unchanged.
